---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Prose
  title="Security — CabSnap"
  description="Where your receipt data lives and who can see it."
  path="/security"
  heading="Security"
>
  <p>
    You are handing an app a picture of everything you spend money on. It is fair
    to ask where that goes.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Draft — needs completion before launch.</strong> The sections below
    must be filled in with the app's actual infrastructure before this page ships.
    Do not publish placeholder security claims; an inaccurate security page is
    worse than no security page.
  </div>

  <h2>Where receipts are stored</h2>
  <p>[CONFIRM: hosting provider, region, and whether images are stored encrypted at rest.]</p>

  <h2>Who can see them</h2>
  <p>[CONFIRM: which staff, if any, can access user receipt images, and under what circumstances.]</p>

  <h2>How data moves</h2>
  <p>[CONFIRM: TLS version for transit, and which third-party services process receipt images for text extraction.]</p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>[CONFIRM: how a user deletes their account and what happens to stored images afterward. Google Play requires an account deletion path.]</p>

  <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
  <p>
    Found something concerning? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
    and we will look at it.
  </p>
</Prose>
